-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSTALL
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Requirements
------------
 - git
 - gcc (>= 4.0)
 - g++
 - make
 - cmake >= 3.10
 - Qt6 (Core, Gui, Widgets and Svg); Qt5 (>= 5.0) is still supported as a fallback
 - libglib >= 2.32.0
 - zlib
 - libusb-1.0 >= 1.0.16
	On FreeBSD, this is an integral part of the FreeBSD libc, not an extra package/library.
	This is part of the standard OpenBSD install (not an extra package), apparently.
 - libboost >= 1.42
 - libfftw3 >= 3.3
 - libpython > 3.2
 - pkg-config >= 0.22


Building and installing
-----------------------

Step1: Installing the requirements:
please check your respective distro's package manager tool if you use other distros

Debian/Ubuntu:
 $ sudo apt install git gcc g++ make cmake qt6-base-dev libqt6svg6-dev libgl1-mesa-dev \
 	libxkbcommon-dev libvulkan-dev libglib2.0-dev zlib1g-dev libusb-1.0-0-dev libboost-dev libfftw3-dev python3-dev libudev-dev pkg-config
 	 	
   How to install qt on ubuntu?
   	qt5: qtbase5-dev,libqt5svg5-dev
   	qt6: qt6-base-dev,libqt6svg6-dev,libgl1-mesa-dev*,libxkbcommon-dev,libvulkan-dev

   The Qt Svg module is not optional: the themes draw all checkboxes, combobox
   arrows and window buttons from SVG files, and without its qsvg plugins those
   controls are simply not painted (the build and the startup log stay clean).

Fedora:
 $ sudo yum install git gcc g++ make cmake pkgconfig glib2-devel \
   zlib-devel libudev-devel libusb1-devel \
   python3-devel qt6-qtbase-devel qt6-qtsvg-devel boost-devel libfftw3-devel

Arch:
 $ pacman -S base-devel git cmake glib2 zlib libusb \
   python boost qt6-base qt6-svg fftw
   
Mac:
  install git
  install hombrew
  brew install gcc
  brew install g++
  brew install make
  brew install cmake
  brew install gettext
  brew install glib
  brew install libusb
  brew install zlib
  brew install boost
  brew install fftw
  brew install python3
  brew install qt
  brew install pkg-config


Step2: Get the DSView source code
 $ git clone https://github.com/Schildkroet/DSView

Step3: Building
 $ make
 $ sudo make install

 In-source builds (`cmake .`) are not supported. `make` configures and builds
 in ./build (executable: build/bin/DSView). Without the wrapper:
 $ cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
 $ cmake --build build -j "$(nproc)"
 $ sudo cmake --install build

See the following wiki page for more (OS-specific) instructions:
 http://sigrok.org/wiki/Building
 
The latest source code:
 https://github.com/Schildkroet/DSView
 
